 Note: for simplicity and also to not alter too much base advciv +/- civ4 behaviour, we only tweak the UNITAIs of the units we produce if these criterion are met, but do not alter war decisions or such, still it seems base advciv or at least now our mod's code picks up well enough on this available stack and uses it seems (although i didn't look in detail). Defense seems to be preserved since we targeted mostly low city empires or ones with mostly defenders (might backfire a bit for large empires so maybe we could make the check stricter but maybe they can gamble a bit early on and bet on them producing enough units midgame to fill all cities, while low city empires would aimed for targetted invasions to attempt to if i may say but anyways etc overcome low city number ideally but anyways etc).
 
+## 53.2.2 (Seemingly greatly enhanced) AI overproducing defenders early on, especially longbowmen but not only, replaced with an early produce more versatile units especially civ-specific ones when defended enough (at least in theory anyways etc) in CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit anyways etc
+
+See screenshots and files about/related(ing? Anyways etc) to this issue in this [google drive folder link](https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1xiDPP6ySpqr61T08iJ9hNKv4IWodcUCq?usp=sharing).
+
+This is an issue that i think has now been significantly improved, and that should make AI stronger (at least in theory, as it doesn't seem always applied, but often enough), so AI is hopefully stronger thanks to this (but check to be sure anyways etc).
+
+The problem was that AI would often produce too many defenders in the early game, which we tried to address in 53.2, but in an autoplay run i tried, hatshepsut ai had both many cities but also somehow most units in the game, which was not covered by our previous fix in 53.2, so she seemingly still produced way too much units.
+
+So i added code to take into account our defense needs as minimally as possible (offense units can defend too especially if we are stronger), but also enhanced and expanded upon the code in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit` to now actually change the actual unit produced to an offensive or more versatile-offense oriented unit, carefully ignoring non default unitais like counter if not the default one (else we'd produce tons of longbowmen but not more versatile units, which is a waste if we are so strong, no need to defend so hard, even if we have many cities to protect, we can still capitalize a bit on our strength i think and make some gains or weaken nearby rivals somehow if we can).
+
+The results are very impressive, hatshepsut ai went from having +/- 30 longbows at turn 130 which was a big waste even if she had 6 cities more or less (didn't count exactly anyways etc) to now 32 war chariots at turn 130!!!! and other units like 9 camel archers, etc.
+
+Although in some other cases it doesn't seem applied, like khmer ai still going for many longbows, despite having bonuses to build other units (didn't check in detail), but should make quite a difference, he seems to have less longbowmen than before changes and quite a few other units like spearmen which i think is good for versatility as well but anyways etc.
+
+While making this new code, i also tried to enforce picking (extra valuing) civ-specific units on the assumptions they are nice (war chariots very cheap and effective for example rather than a horse archer), and avoid otherwise weak units to avoid high unit costs and low effectiveness of the military anyways etc.
+
+I then tried another autoplay run and it was very very brutal, with ewuare ai having 150+ cavalry at turn 260 (in a standard monarch pangea normal game speed map if i am not mistaken but anyways etc) more or less and other units in lower number but anyways etc where he won! Despite not having train percent discounts per era anymore in advciv-sas as of now! I think the good offensive start helped convert it easier to a middle game offensive stack although i didn't check in detail but anyways etc.
+
+So overall very good results it seems!
+
+While doing this, i also enhanced the code of the fallback unit choice `CvCity::doTurn()` in as of now [51 - (Worked around / fixed) Massive seemingly base advciv +/- civ4 issue if i'm not mistaken of many cities entering no production early for 1 or several turns many times during the game early (and possibly later this is why many cities have a process rather than no production, as processes are not available early and are listed among fallbacks if production fails it seems but check to be sure anyways etc)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#51---worked-around--fixed-massive-seemingly-base-advciv---civ4-issue-if-im-not-mistaken-of-many-cities-entering-no-production-early-for-1-or-several-turns-many-times-during-the-game-early-and-possibly-later-this-is-why-many-cities-have-a-process-rather-than-no-production-as-processes-are-not-available-early-and-are-listed-among-fallbacks-if-production-fails-it-seems-but-check-to-be-sure-anyways-etc) with quite similar logic as well (actually improved it while doing changes here anyways etc and then ported these improvements in a relevant way but anyways etc to the chooseunit function but anyways etc).
+
+Note: i noticed during testing rare crashes at turn 90-100 in a few autoplay maps, disappears after reloading a recent save file, so did not dig further, but i found for info in the .dmp file with windbg which i don't know too much about the culprit to likely be `CvSelectionGroup::plot` or something near it, but check if accurate, and since it is only a ["temporary" crash](/README.md#temporary-crashes), not investigating further anyways etc.
+
